# Review: ChessComPlugin

The plugin implements the whole spec. `ChessComAccount.Account` has every listed field, a child games
feed and the `chess.com` foreign key; the create form asks only for a username; `SyncGames` loads the
player profile, walks the monthly archives, imports each game as a `Game` with a `Chess.State`
variant and skips games whose `game/<uuid>` key is already in the feed. `sync-games.test.ts` covers
import and dedup against a stubbed chess.com API. The article lists games in a masonry of
`CardContent` surfaces.

The gaps are test coverage, not behaviour: nothing tests the create-object path, the foreign key on
the account, the applied profile fields or the article. Two small differences: the username is
lower-cased before it is stored and keyed, and creating an account also schedules a first sync.

Of 14 items: 6 done, 6 untested, 0 partial, 0 diverged, 2 missing.

